// SISALv3 database schema — DBML
// Generated from sisalv3.sql (mysqldump, InnoDB, utf8mb4) in this same folder.
// Paste directly into https://dbdiagram.io to render the ER diagram.
// 21 published tables + 8 draft v3.1 tables (see bottom section).
//
// Changes since the 2026-08-20 snapshot:
// - Added `not null` to FK columns that should always be populated (entity.site_id,
//   composite_link_entity, entity_link_reference, dating.entity_id, dating_lamina.entity_id,
//   sample.entity_id, project_link_entity) — these were previously nullable by omission.
// - entity_person renamed to entity_link_person, matching the _link_ naming convention
//   already used by composite_link_entity/entity_link_reference.
// - database_release.previous_release changed from varchar to a real self-referencing FK
//   (int, ref: > database_release.release_id) — was a free-text label before.
// - New code_artifact type `lcc_product` (+ database_release.lcc_artifact_id) — a third
//   reusable pipeline alongside agemodel/downsampling, for the entity.copernicus_lcc
//   land-cover classification. (Not to be confused with the pre-existing
//   copernicus_lcc_enum used by entity.copernicus_lcc itself — different thing.)
// - New `projects` table (+ project_person, project_link_entity, project_type_enum):
//   project promoted from a plain varchar on database_release to a first-class entity,
//   with its own DOI, status, linked entities, and linked people.
// - database_release.project and .is_subset REMOVED. Deliberate: database_release no
//   longer links to `projects` directly — which project(s) fed a release is derived via
//   project_link_entity + entity.added_in_release_id, not stored redundantly. See
//   release-management framework.md.
// - role_enum renamed to contributor_role_enum (shared by release_person.role and
//   project_person.role).

